Test: prefer-regexp-exec >> invalid
Code:
  1 |
  2 |             'something'.match(new RegExp('thing'));
    |             ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ [1]
  3 |             'something'.match(new RegExp('thing', 'i'));
    |             ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ [2]
  4 |             

[1] Use the `RegExp#exec()` method instead.
[2] Use the `RegExp#exec()` method instead.
---


Test: prefer-regexp-exec >> invalid
Code:
  1 |
  2 |             function fn(pattern) {
  3 |                 const text = 'something';
  4 |                 // The pattern is known to be a string, so it contributes no flags.
  5 |                 text.match(new RegExp(`^${pattern}$`));
    |                 ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ [1]
  6 |                 text.match(new RegExp(pattern + ''));
    |                 ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ [2]
  7 |                 // The flags argument takes precedence over the flags of the pattern.
  8 |                 text.match(new RegExp(pattern, 'i'));
    |                 ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ [3]
  9 |             }
 10 |             

[1] Use the `RegExp#exec()` method instead.
[2] Use the `RegExp#exec()` method instead.
[3] Use the `RegExp#exec()` method instead.
---
